    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=Qpt8e": {
      "title": "Associate Director Resilience",
      "description": "Associate Director Resilience - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Associate Director Resilience Associate Director Resilience Lead AUT’s university-wide resilience, emergency management and business continuity programme Embed embedding a strong culture of preparedness and resilience Full time, permanent position based on AUT’s city campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT consists of three distinct campuses as well as minor sub-entities. Its estate is made up of 60+ buildings valued at some $1.5 billion and covers some 30Ha of land. Within that profile is two halls of residence with 500+ residents. This role is within the Estates Division that is tasked with the protection and enhancement of that environment. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We're looking for an experienced leader to take on the role of Associate Director, Resilience - a position central to the university's emergency management and business continuity program.  This role is responsible for driving a culture of resilience and building a culture that enables our people, systems, and services to adapt and thrive in the face of disruption.  We are seeking an experienced, strategic, and forward-thinking professional to lead this transformation.  This is a senior leadership role focused on embedding a culture of resilience across AUT - beginning with strategic engagement at governance level and cascading down. This role is responsible leading AUT’s business continuity and emergency management functions, ensuring we are prepared to manage risk, respond effectively to disruption, and recover quickly. In this role, you will: Champion resilience as an organisational priority, embedding a whole-university approach that aligns with our strategic goals. Design and implement systems that build preparedness into the culture, from policy through to everyday practice. Lead and deliver training programs that empower staff with the capability and confidence to act decisively in times of crisis. Strengthen external partnerships with key agencies, including Auckland Emergency Management and NEMA, ensuring AUT is aligned with best practice and national standards. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: A strategic mindset and strong leadership presence, with a track record of influencing at a senior level. Strong expertise in emergency management, business continuity, and organisational resilience. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills – able to connect across academic, operational, and external audiences. A proactive and collaborative approach to building capability and confidence across a complex organisation. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: to be agreed with the successful applicant For further information : Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant - caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 16 October 2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96666 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96666 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 16 Oct 2026 17:00 Expertise Administration, Executive, Management & Planning Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10578 - Associate Director Resilience.pdf Posted on 25 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=slX9e": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse",
      "description": "Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse - School of Nursing (perm, 0.6FTE) - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse - School of Nursing (perm, 0.6FTE) Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse - School of Nursing (perm, 0.6FTE) Culturally responsive practice Teach & mentor future nurse Permanent, part-time (0.6FTE annualised) role based at AUT's North Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The School of Nursing at AUT has recently been established as its own school, recognising the significant impact and achievement of nursing at AUT as part of a wider promotion of clearer school identities and disciplinary alignments (whilst also enhancing faculty-level connectivity and addressing school size disparities). The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi The School of Nursing has a part-time (0.6FTE), permanent opportunity for a motivated Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse to join the school.  This position is annualised. We require a nurse educator to fulfil the clinical position. The successful applicant will be expected to contribute to clinical education in the Bachelor of Health Science (Nursing) and Master of Nursing Science programmes.   To be considered for the position applicants must have a minimum of a PG certificate in a qualification relating to Nursing.  There is an expectation that the appointee will contribute to the development of clinical learning within nursing at AUT. Applicants will have a current NCNZ practising certificate and recent New Zealand clinical experience. They will embrace the vision and values of the school and commit to ongoing professional development supported by the AUT staff development programme. The position will work alongside students including Māori and Pacific students so a high level of cultural sensitivity is desired, along with knowledge of kawa and tikanga Māori and mātauranga Māori (Māori knowledge). We embrace practice-led, research-informed approaches to teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities. Your contributions to programme and course development will support our continuous-improvement focus. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive .  Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. We welcome applications from registered nurses. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV please also submit: a cover letter explaining which specific role is of interest, why AUT and how your experience aligns with some, or all, of the selection criteria in the Position Description a teaching and/or research statement (if relevant) (1 page each max) Please feel free to add any further comments you feel may also support your application. All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $96,000 - $101,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) - pro rata For academic enquiries: Contact Jane Marshall, Registered Nurse/Clinical Educator, jane.marshall@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 12 October 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96788 This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checks as part of the Children’s Act 2014 . At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96788 Location (s) North Campus Employment type (s) Part-time permanent Closes on 12 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Clinical Educator Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10975 - Clinical Educator.pdf Posted on 28 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=PiY9e": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator/Registered Nurse",
