    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=Shh5e": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Addictions Programme - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturer - Addictions Programme Lecturer - Addictions Programme Join a growing Addictions academic team supporting New Zealand's health workforce Contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching in Addictions Support innovative teaching, curriculum development and student success Permanent, full-time position based at AUT North Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together and make a genuine difference for students, communities and society. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti o Waitangi plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic circumstances and accessibility needs. The School of Community and Public Health is committed to improving health and wellbeing through excellence in education, scholarship and community engagement. The Mental Health and Addictions Programme delivers specialist undergraduate and postgraduate education that supports the development of Aotearoa New Zealand's mental health and addiction workforce. The programme works closely with health sector partners to deliver contemporary, practice-informed education that responds to current and emerging workforce needs. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Lecturer (Teaching and Learning) to make a significant contribution through teaching and service within the Mental Health and Addictions Programme. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and postgraduate teaching and support the ongoing development of high-quality educational experiences across the programme portfolio. Responsibilities include: Teaching and assessment across Addictions courses Curriculum design, review and enhancement Development of innovative teaching and learning resources Student support, supervision and academic guidance Course coordination and moderation activities Engagement with professional and industry stakeholders Contribution to programme and School service activities We are particularly interested in applicants who can contribute to teaching in: Addictions Mental Health Health Workforce Development Contemporary Professional Practice We embrace practice-led and scholarship-informed approaches to teaching that create transformative student experiences and strengthen communities. Contributing to programme development, innovative teaching methods, assessment design, marking and the development of educational resources are key aspects of this role. You will also be expected to maintain industry relevance through engagement with professional organisations and sector partners. Please refer to the Position Description for further information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . for career-path roles - add: We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds, and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . About you | Ko wai koe We are looking for an educator who is passionate about Addictions education and committed to supporting student success, workforce development and excellence in professional practice. Qualifications A postgraduate qualification in Mental Health, Addictions, Social Work, Nursing, Psychology, Psychotherapy, Counselling or a related discipline Current dapaanz registration A doctoral qualification, or progress towards one, would be advantageous Teaching Experience teaching and supporting adult learners Experience in curriculum development and innovative teaching practice Ability to create engaging and inclusive learning environments Experience supervising, mentoring or supporting students Scholarship and Professional Practice Demonstrated commitment to maintaining professional relevance and industry engagement Ability to apply evidence-informed practice within teaching and learning Interest in educational scholarship and continuous improvement Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey . Ability to work effectively with diverse students, communities and stakeholder groups How to Apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit: A cover letter outlining your interest in the role and how your experience aligns with the position A statement describing how you meet the key selection criteria Evidence of teaching effectiveness and educational innovation is welcome Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $86,000 - $102,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact Jo Appleby, Head of Department - Psychotherapy & Counselling, jo.appleby@aut.ac.nz Closing Date: 13 October 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference: 96376 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96376 Location (s) North Campus, South Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 13 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Academic, Academic Management, Adjunct Professor, Associate Professor, Clinical Educator, Lecturer, Midwife, Professor, Research, Senior Lecturer, Teaching Assistant Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10882 - SCPH Lecturer (Addictions).pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 29 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=mWm6e": {
      "title": "School Manager",
      "description": "School Manager - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies School Manager School Manager Provide strategic and operational leadership within the School, partnering closely with the Head of School and School Leadership Team Lead financial, people and resource management, ensuring effective planning, compliance and delivery across the School Drive operational improvement and strategic projects, including process improvement and digital transformation Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's Akoranga or City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. About the Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences AUT’s Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences is a vibrant, interdisciplinary academic community committed to improving health, wellbeing and environmental sustainability locally and globally. The Faculty brings together leading educators, researchers and practitioners across health sciences, public health, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, food science, chemistry, biology, biomedical science, and environmental science, with a strong emphasis on applied learning and real-world impact. Staff benefit from close links with industry, iwi, communities and government, opportunities for collaborative and translational research, and a culture that values innovation, equity and social responsibility. The Faculty offers an engaging, supportive environment for talented academics who want their teaching and research to make a meaningful difference in Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is a senior leadership opportunity to provide strategic and operational oversight across two Schools within AUT's Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences. Reporting to the Director – Faculty Operations and working closely with the Head of School and School Leadership Team, you will provide leadership across the School's financial, administrative, people and operational functions. You will be a key point of contact for operational matters, providing advice and support that enables the School to achieve its strategic and academic objectives. You will lead operational planning, budget management, workforce and HR processes, facilities and resource management, and ensure effective systems and processes are in place to support the School's activities. You'll also contribute to faculty-wide priorities and initiatives through special projects and portfolio responsibilities. A key part of the role will be identifying opportunities to improve how the School operates, including process improvement and responsible use of digital tools and technology. You'll work collaboratively across the School, Faculty and wider University with stakeholders including People and Culture, Finance and Procurement, Estates and ICT. This role requires sound judgement, strong relationship management and the ability to work confidently across a complex tertiary environment. You'll bring a practical, solutions-focused approach while balancing strategic priorities with the day-to-day operational needs of the School. You will also play an important leadership role in embedding AUT's Te Aronui framework, values and commitment to creating equitable and mana-enhancing outcomes. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff. About you | Ko wai koe As an experienced operations leader, you'll bring the ability to balance strategic thinking with strong operational delivery. You'll be comfortable working across a broad portfolio of financial, people, administrative and organisational responsibilities and able to build trusted relationships across a complex organisation. You'll have strong judgement, initiative and problem-solving skills, with the ability to influence and work collaboratively with a wide range of stakeholders. Experience working within a tertiary environment would be highly valued. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting equity, diversity and inclusion initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant tertiary qualification and significant experience in operations management within a medium to large organisation Experience in financial management, budgeting and resource planning, with a sound understanding of accounting principles and processes Strong people leadership, organisational and administrative skills, with experience managing complex HR processes Excellent communication, relationship management and influencing skills, with the ability to work effectively across a diverse stakeholder group Experience leading projects, change initiatives and process improvements High digital fluency, including experience with financial management systems and Microsoft 365 applications Strategic thinking and strong problem-solving skills, combined with a practical and solutions-focused approach A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: To be agreed with the successful candidate. Salary Range | Ngā Utu: $110,000 - $131,000 commensurate with the skills and experience of the successful candidate. For further information: Contact Caroline Cranston, AUT Recruitment Consultant – caroline.cranston@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 18th October 2026 at 5pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96459 Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96459 Location (s) North Campus, City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 18 Oct 2026 17:00 Expertise Administration Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11053 - School Manager.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 29 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=Pnk8e": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturer Lecturer Seeking emerging academic expertise in management, leadership, and the future of work. Permanent, full-time role based at AUT’s City Campus in central Auckland. Join a department focused on contemporary management and organisational challenges. Build your academic career in a supportive, interdisciplinary environment. Contribute to practical, engaging teaching that connects theory with current organisational issues. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT's Management, Technology, and Organisation (MTO) Department is part of our Business School . Our School holds two of the most prestigious global business school accreditations: EQUIS and AACSB, attesting to the quality of its programmes and research. In line with AUT's positioning as a university of opportunity and New Zealand's only university of technology, we care about student success. We embrace practice-led and research-informed approaches to teaching, to optimise the student experience, and we pride ourselves on our significant industry connections and opportunities for work-integrated learning. Our research is internationally recognised, with particular expertise aligned to themes of inclusive work and wellbeing, responsible business, and digital futures and innovation. To learn more about MTO, please click here: Management, Technology and Organisation The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi MTO has a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Early Career Lecturer to make a significant impact and develop their career in teaching and service. We are particularly interested in applicants who can contribute to our teaching in general management, leadership, and human resource management . The ability to bring Māori perspectives and mātauranga Māori to these topics, while also engaging with broader Indigenous perspectives, would be an advantage. We embrace practice-led, research-informed approaches to teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities. Your contributions to programme and course development will support our continuous-improvement focus. You will teach across programmes as assigned by the Head of Department and be comfortable using digital resources to enhance learning. Contributing to designing study programmes, advancing pedagogical approaches, designing innovative teaching methods, marking assignments and developing teaching materials, among other things, also form key parts of the role.  You will also be expected to conduct pedagogical research and must maintain industry relevance by engaging with external organisations Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. We welcome applications from Early Career academics. The selection criteria sought are: Qualification: A completed research Masters Degree in Management or a related field Enrolled in a PhD in Management or a related field. Current professional or industry certifications relevant to areas such as management, HR or leadership would be desirable. The ability to bring Māori perspectives and mātauranga Māori to these areas would also be an advantage. Teaching: An early career academic will ideally have at least some previous teaching assistant experience. More experienced candidates will have previous lecturing experience, evidence of curriculum development and preferably experience supervising applied, industry-based or work-integrated learning projects. Scholarship and Professional Practice: An expressed specific desire to be a teaching-focused academic who will undertake activity as specified to maintain professional currency. Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a complete list of publications and grant acquisitions): please submit a) a cover letter which explains why this particular role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) a statement addressing how you feel you meet all of the criteria above. Along with your full academic CV, please also submit: a cover letter explaining which specific role is of interest, why AUT and how your experience aligns with the selection criteria we're seeking above; Evidence of satisfactory student evaluations and innovation in teaching (2 pages max). Any other evidence of teaching experience. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: January/February 2027 Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $86,000 - $102,000 per annum (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact the Head of Department of Management, Organisation and Technology, Associate Professor Peter McGhee, peter.mcghee@aut.ac.nz Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 14th October 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96657 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96657 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 15 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (Less than 2 years), Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 1684 Teaching Path Lecturer (1).pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 30 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
