    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=SKJ9e": {
      "title": "Exam Invigilators",
      "description": "Exam Invigilators - Allied - Timesheet - Hourly paid - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Exam Invigilators - Allied - Timesheet - Hourly paid Exam Invigilators - Allied - Timesheet - Hourly paid The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are now recruiting a limited number of Exam Invigilators for the 2026/2027 academic year . This is an excellent opportunity for individuals who are reliable, detail-oriented, and committed to supporting the integrity of the examination process at AUT. As an Exam Invigilator you will be responsible for ensuring that examinations and Handback/Review Sessions are properly conducted in accordance with the AUT Examination Rules and Regulations and under the direction of the University Examinations Office (UEO) or other academic staff. You must be comfortable working independently, following detailed instructions, and contributing positively within a large and diverse team. About you | Ko wai koe MUST be available for both morning and afternoon exam sessions on most weekdays, when required, during the below peak periods: From 21 October to 6 November 2026 Additional sessions may occasionally occur outside these dates MUST be able to work across at least two of AUT’s campuses – City, North, or South Have previous invigilation or teaching/lecturing/administration experience Have basic computer skills and be confident using digital tools as required Must have a satisfactory level of physical fitness and be able to carry the exam box to the exam room and stand for extended periods Must be responsible, reliable, and punctual Have strong references and a professional work ethic Please do not apply unless you meet the criteria above. Preference will be given to applicants who are available and fully committed to working with the Exam Invigilation team throughout the 2026 academic year and 2027. You must also be available to join us for a short interview and a Compulsory Training Session . Dates to be confirmed following shortlisting. All applicants must be eligible to work in New Zealand. Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $30.34 per hour Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96766 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 12 October 2026 at 11:55 pm Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is bold and unapologetically different, centred on students and grounded in Knowledge that Works driven by talented, progressive people. We are New Zealand’s newest university, ranked 5-stars by QS Universities 2025 and a place of opportunity where more than 26,000 students with talent and potential succeed, supported by a community of more than 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. Built on collaboration, shared purpose and the values of Pono (fact, truth, reality, integrity), Tika (acting accordingly, doing what is needed, ethical expression), and Aroha (empathy, care, compassion). AUT offers an innovative, forward-thinking environment where committed people work together to improve outcomes for students, communities, and the world. AUT recognises the importance of Te Tiriti, Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership, and contribution across our university and is committed to creating environments where these communities can thrive. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96766 Location (s) North Campus, City Campus, South Campus Employment type (s) Casual (hourly paid) Closes on 12 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Exam Invigilator Experience level (s) Experienced (Less than 2 years) More details (document) Candidate Information Guide Posted on 05 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
