    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=Yk3be": {
      "title": "Technical Services Manager",
      "description": "Technical Services Manager – Built Environment - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Technical Services Manager – Built Environment Technical Services Manager – Built Environment Lead a technical team supporting practical learning, research and industry projects. Combine specialist expertise with hands-on leadership of laboratories, equipment and services. Full-time permanent| AUT City Campus, Auckland. Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Within the Faculty of Design and Creative Technologies, the School of Future Environments brings together teaching and research focused on the environments we design, build and inhabit. Our technical team supports this work through specialist facilities, equipment and practical expertise that help staff and students turn ideas into practice. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are seeking an experienced Technical Services Manager to lead day-to-day technical operations in Built Environment, including the Construction Lab. Reporting to the Senior Manager – Technical Services, you will combine practical technical expertise with people leadership to provide safe, reliable support for teaching, research and approved commercial projects. You will coordinate staff and resources, support complex technical work, and work closely with academic colleagues to plan delivery around changing requirements. Your responsibilities will include: Leading and developing technical staff through clear priorities, coaching and constructive feedback. Providing specialist advice, demonstrations and practical support to students, researchers and staff, including the construction and installation of research and client projects. Coordinating equipment procurement, maintenance and repairs, and advising on the design and use of technical spaces. Leading local health, safety and wellbeing practices, including risk controls, induction, training and emergency readiness. Managing loan-out operations and the SISO inventory management system, and leading commercial projects as required. You will collaborate with Estates, HSW, Finance, suppliers and industry partners, and act as a delegate for the Senior Manager during absences. Through inclusive leadership, equitable access to technical support and ongoing cultural learning, you will help give practical effect to Te Aronui, AUT’s Te Tiriti Framework. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Explore AUT’s staff benefits About you | Ko wai koe You are an experienced technical professional and people leader who enjoys working alongside a team. You can resolve complex technical problems, manage projects and priorities, organize competing demands and build effective relationships with students, academics and professional colleagues. You bring sound judgement, financial literacy and a practical approach to improving services. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: A relevant undergraduate degree with extensive subsequent relevant experience. Substantial experience in a relevant technical setting, with extensive knowledge of equipment used in built environment laboratories or related technical facilities. Experience managing or supervising technical teams, coordinating resources and supporting staff development. Project management experience and the ability to analyse complex technical problems and develop practical, innovative solutions. Knowledge and experience of implementing health and safety requirements in a technical environment. Strong communication, interpersonal and digital skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, and to supporting AUT’s Te Aronui journey. A postgraduate qualification, a first aid certificate and extensive specialist experience in one of the School’s technical fields are desirable. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter explaining why this role and AUT are of interest, and how you meet the key criteria listed above. All applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start date: As soon as possible Salary range | Ngā Utu: $93,000 - $114,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information: Please send your enquiry to Kristina Bojin <kristina.bojin@aut.ac.nz> Closing date | Te rā aukati: 20th October 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96908 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96908 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 20 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Executive, Management & Planning, Technician Experience level (s) Management More details (document) PD 1365 - Technical Services Manager.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 06 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=IQE9e": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Perioperative Practice - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Perioperative Practice Lecturer/Senior Lecturer - Perioperative Practice Seeking clinical and academic expertise in the Post Anaesthetic Care Unit (PACU) Actively contribute to collaborative research in healthcare Be part of a forward-focused national programme integrating simulation, clinical expertise, and innovative teaching approaches Permanent, full-time (1.0 FTE) appointment at Lecturer or Senior Lecturer level based at AUT's South Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT's School of Acute and Primary Health AUT's Perioperative Practice department is part of our School of Acute and Primary Health. The School is a leader in health education in Aotearoa New Zealand, delivering high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in oral health, paramedicine, midwifery and perioperative practice. These disciplines span the acute and primary care continuum, preparing graduates to work across diverse healthcare settings, from acute and emergency response, pre-operative, intra-operative and post-operative care to contributions in community-based and preventative healthcare services. The school’s unique combination of programmes reflects its commitment to integrated, person-centred healthcare that is responsive to both immediate and long-term needs. The School is part of our dynamic Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences . To learn more about our Health Sciences departments , please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/health-sciences The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have a permanent, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunity for a motivated Lecturer or Senior Lecturer to make a meaningful impact and further develop their career in teaching and research. We are looking for an experienced academic or registered health professional with experience in PACU.  The ideal candidate will provide specialist expertise in the development and delivery of education across areas of perioperative practice that have traditionally been led by perioperative and emergency nursing professionals. You will also contribute to research activity, supervision and support the ongoing development of the programme. We are particularly interested in applicants who can contribute to our teaching and research in: Perioperative nursing Critical and acute care practice Post anaesthesia care Simulation-based education in healthcare Research and evidence-based practice in healthcare We embrace practice-led, research-informed approaches to teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities. Your contributions to programme and course development will support our continuous-improvement focus. You will teach across programmes as assigned by the Head of Department and be comfortable using digital resources to enhance learning. You will publish actively in your specialised field/s. Research at AUT i s central to our mission, driving innovation, informing teaching and creating real-world impact for communities, industry and society. Over time, successful candidates are expected to seek and attract external research funding, engage with government, business, professional bodies and the community, and contribute to school/faculty activities. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds and guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff. https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. We welcome applications from Health Sciences academics. The selection criteria sought are: Qualification: A PhD in Health Sciences (or a related field) or postgraduate qualification in a relevant clinical field Registration (or eligibility for registration) with a New Zealand regulatory authority. A current Annual Practising Certificate (or eligibility for an Annual Practising Certificate) Relevant clinical experience. Research: An early career academic will have the basis of a solid research pipeline and a primary-authored research paper available. Evidence of proactively pursuing external research income is desirable. (Lecturers) Evidence of securing or contributing to external research income is desirable. (Senior Lecturers) Teaching: An early career academic will ideally have at least some previous teaching assistant experience. More experienced candidates will have previous lecturing experience, evidence of curriculum development and preferably experience supervising Masters and/or PhD students. Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a full publication list and grant acquisitions, if applicable); please also submit: A cover letter which explains why this particular role (and AUT) is of interest and how your experience aligns with some, or all, of the selection criteria we're seeking above; A research statement (1 page max); Relevant evidence of satisfactory student evaluations and innovation in teaching (2 pages max). A nominated journal or conference article All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: February / March 2027 Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: Lecturer - $96,685 - $115,067 (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) Senior Lecturer - $118,458 - $154,891 (appointment level and salary commensurate with skills and experience) For academic enquiries: Contact Megan Richardson, Head of Department – Perioperative Practice megan.richardson@aut.ac.nz. For recruitment enquiries, please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499. Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 3rd November 2026, at 11:55 pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96752 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96752 Location (s) South Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 03 Nov 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer, Senior Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11066 - Lecturer Senior Lecturer - Perioperative Practice RN focus.pdf Candidate Information Guide Posted on 06 Oct 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    }
